#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:136
#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:141
msgid "Email Design"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:137
msgid "These settings style every email HivePress and its extensions send, so the plain messages arrive wrapped in a branded template instead. Preview any email with your design applied in the list above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:142
msgid "Apply the design to outgoing emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:143
msgid "Wraps every email HivePress sends in the template chosen below. Untick to send plain emails exactly as HivePress does on its own; previews and test sends keep working either way. Leave this off if you have already designed your emails by hand, or the two designs will sit on top of each other."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:150
msgid "Design Template"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:151
msgid "The overall look of the email. Clean and Minimal stay out of the way; Boxed puts the message on a rounded card; Bold, Banner and Panel are fully styled, turning a plain link in the message into a button, and Banner and Panel also show the subject as a heading. Preview any email above to see the difference."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:163
msgid "Accent Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:164
msgid "Used for the card border, the subject heading, buttons and links inside the email - and for the header bar on Bold and Banner unless you set a header colour below. Paste a 6-digit hex code such as #2b6cb0, or pick one; empty uses a neutral blue."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:171
msgid "Header Bar Colour"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the default dark colour Panel uses, as a hex code.
#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:173
#, php-format
msgid "Only for templates that have a coloured bar across the top - Bold, Banner and Panel. Empty follows the template: the accent colour for Bold and Banner, %s for Panel. The site name and heading on the bar switch between white and dark text on their own, whichever reads better against the colour you pick."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:180
msgid "Background Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:181
msgid "The page colour behind the email card. Paste a 6-digit hex code, or pick one; empty uses a light grey."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:188
msgid "Text Colour"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:189
msgid "The colour of the words in the body of the email. Empty uses a dark grey that stays readable on a white card."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:196
msgid "Logo Image"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:197
msgid "Shown at the top of every email. Use the Choose image button to pick one from your Media Library, or paste an image address. Empty shows your site name as text instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:205
msgid "Logo Width (pixels)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:206
msgid "The displayed width of the logo image. The height scales to match. Empty goes back to 180."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:216
msgid "Logo Position"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:217
msgid "Where the logo or site name sits in the header, whichever template you have chosen."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:234
msgid "Left"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:235
msgid "Centre"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:236
msgid "Right"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:241
msgid "Footer Text"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: the year token, 2: the site name token, 3: the user name token. All three are filled in automatically and must be left exactly as they appear.
#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:244
#, php-format
msgid "Small print at the bottom of every email. %1$s and %2$s fill themselves in, and any token the email itself offers works here too, so %3$s greets the person receiving it. Line breaks are kept. A link, bold and italic are allowed. Empty means no footer at all."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:274
#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:279
msgid "Delivery Log"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:275
msgid "Keeps a short record of the emails your site sends, shown at the bottom of this screen. It is what tells \"the email never sent\" apart from \"it sent and did not arrive\", which is the difference between a problem with your site and a problem with the inbox it was going to. The record includes the address each email went to, so it is personal data: keep it short, and clear it when you no longer need it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:280
msgid "Record emails as they are sent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:281
msgid "Untick to record nothing at all. Anything already recorded stays until you clear it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:288
msgid "Entries to Keep"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:289
msgid "Once this many are recorded, the oldest drops off as each new one arrives. Empty goes back to 100."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:301
msgid "Removing the Plugin"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:302
msgid "What happens if you ever delete this plugin. WordPress shows a generic warning that deleting a plugin also deletes its data; for this plugin that only applies if you tick the box below. Emails you have customised belong to HivePress itself and are never deleted either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:306
msgid "Delete All Data"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:307
msgid "Delete all data when this plugin is deleted"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:308
msgid "Removes every Email Studio setting when the plugin is deleted from the Plugins screen. This cannot be undone. Leave unticked to keep your settings for a future reinstall; deactivating never removes anything either way."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:334
msgid "WooCommerce styles its own emails, so by default this plugin leaves them alone and only lists them. You can hand WooCommerce your colours, logo and footer wording so its layout matches yours, or go further and send WooCommerce emails inside the same wrapper as every HivePress email. Use Preview on any WooCommerce email to compare the layouts before you change anything."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the name of another plugin that also designs WooCommerce emails.
#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:346
#, php-format
msgid "You also have %s active, which designs WooCommerce emails as well. Use one or the other, not both."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:352
#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:357
msgid "WooCommerce Emails"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:358
msgid "Use my design for WooCommerce emails too"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:359
msgid "Applies your accent colour, background, text colour, logo and footer to WooCommerce's own email template. WooCommerce keeps its own layout, so an order table still looks like an order table; only the branding around it changes. Your WooCommerce email settings are left untouched, so unticking this puts everything back. The wrapper layouts below apply the colours whether or not this is ticked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:365
msgid "WooCommerce Email Layout"
msgstr ""

#: includes/components/class-hpes-settings.php:366
msgid "\"WooCommerce layout\" sends WooCommerce's own frame: its header, its heading and its footer. \"Email Studio wrapper\" lifts the message out of that frame and sends it inside your design template, with WooCommerce's heading at the top of the message; the order table keeps its WooCommerce styling. \"Message body only\" does the same without the heading. Previews and test sends use whichever you choose here."
msgstr ""

